+---
+
+## 0. 2026-09-06 — v2 forecaster integrated (read this first)
+
+The bundle the service loads by default is now **`outputs/mlcc_v2/model_bundle`**
+(`mlcc-pilot-1.1`, same bundle id `b5553f6f7032092e-s26170` because it was
+trained from the same data files). It contains everything the v1 bundle had plus
+one model, **`xgboost_v2`**, which won internal validation and is therefore the
+default forecast. The v1 bundle is untouched and still loads
+(`SIH_MLCC_BUNDLE_DIR=outputs/mlcc_v1/model_bundle`).
+
+| | v1 default (persistence) | v2 default (`xgboost_v2`) |
+|---|---|---|
+| internal validation, normalized MAE | 0.1795 | **0.1625** |
+| untouched test batches (2,400 parts), normalized MAE | 0.1531 | **0.1348** (0.0715 µA) |
+| test: point forecast flags an observed crossing | 14 of 166 (5 false) | **43 of 166** (19 false) |
+| test: latent crossings caught by the forecast, excluding tester faults | 2 | **31** |
+| fresh 4,000-part set generated by Codex, normalized MAE | 0.1585 | **0.1409** |
+| shifted-condition stress set | 0.1213 | **0.1173** |
+| low-prevalence stress set (almost no defects) | **0.0112** | 0.0208 |
+
+What `xgboost_v2` is: XGBoost with an absolute-error objective trained on the
+correction over persistence (the 24 h value is the base margin), using only the
+ten leakage-derived 0/24 h features, with a quiet-part gate: a part whose 24 h
+level and drift are both within 2 robust standard deviations of its batch keeps
+the plain 24 h value (chosen on training folds: healthy-part MAE 0.0128 vs
+0.0165; bagging was tried and dropped). v1's XGBoost lost because squared error
+inflates healthy forecasts by about 0.12 of the limit; the v2 objective does not.
+Details, diagnostics and the predeclared comparison: `docs/CLAUDE_FORECAST_V2_HANDOFF.md`
+and `outputs/claude_forecast_v2/`. Codex's independent evaluation of the same
+candidate: `outputs/codex_ml_v2_review/` in the main project.
+
+**Interval change.** `xgboost_v2` carries a stratified asymmetric interval
+(strata on the 24 h slope robust z, margins from signed residuals on the
+calibration batches). `prediction_lower`/`prediction_upper` are each one-sided
+90 % bounds, so the pair is an **80 %** interval (`interval_nominal_coverage:
+0.8`, `upper_bound_nominal_level: 0.9`); the wider two-sided 90 % pair is in
+`prediction_lower_two_sided`/`prediction_upper_two_sided`. On the test batches
+the reported pair covered 83.0 % and the upper bound held for 91.9 %. The
+decision rule is unchanged: MONITOR when `prediction_upper` reaches the limit,
+which now means "about a one-in-ten chance of ending above the limit". Other
+models keep the v1 symmetric radius and `interval_nominal_coverage: 0.9`.
+
+**Contract: additive only.** New optional fields on `forecast`:
+`interval_stratum`, `upper_bound_nominal_level`, `prediction_lower_two_sided`,
+`prediction_upper_two_sided`; on `xgboost_explanation`: `explained_model`
+(`xgboost_v2` when it produced the forecast, `xgboost` for the v1 candidate).
+`available_models` gains `xgboost_v2`. Schema version stays `1.0.0`.
+
+**Verified on this machine (Python 3.12, locked library versions):**
+
+| Check | Result |
+|---|---|
+| full suite | **273 passed** (v1: 230; +38 forecast_v2 tests, +4 prototype tests, +1 API test) |
+| `scripts/compare_api_vs_core.py outputs/mlcc_v1/demo_early.csv` | 0 mismatches on 12 fields, for `xgboost_v2` and for `persistence` |
+| live `uvicorn` + `/health/ready` | 200, all checksums (now four artifacts) and versions pass |
+| live `POST /screen` with `demo_early.csv` + `demo_outcomes.csv` | 200, 800 scored / 0 unscored, 2.8 s; ACCEPT 714 · MONITOR 34 · RETEST 33 · ENGINEER_REVIEW 19 |
+| demo reveal (800 parts, 43 cross at 168 h) | 17 of 43 flagged non-ACCEPT; 7 by the point forecast, 17 by the upper bound; v2 normalized MAE 0.131 vs persistence 0.147 |
+| `docs/backend/sample_response.json`, `openapi.json`, `extrapolation_report.csv` | regenerated from the v2 run |
+| ungated bundle `xgboost_v2` vs Codex's independent evaluation of the same candidate (`outputs/codex_ml_v2_review/test_predictions.csv`, 2,400 test parts) | identical to 2e-16 (the gate was added afterwards) |
+
+Files changed for this integration: `src/sih26170/mlcc_prototype.py` (core,
+additive: `xgboost_v2` model class, stratified interval helpers, compatible
+loading of 1.0 bundles), new `src/sih26170/forecast_v2.py`, `api/config.py`
+(default bundle path), `api/schemas.py` and `api/service_mlcc.py` (new optional
+fields), `prediction/mlcc_engine.py` (verify every declared artifact),
+`scripts/{demo_screen,compare_api_vs_core,export_extrapolation,score_mlcc_prototype}.py`
+(bundle path / model choices), tests, docs, `outputs/mlcc_v2/model_bundle/`.
 
